        .modal-dialog(role="document").modal-dialog-centered
            .modal-content
                .modal-header
                    h5.modal-title Torsion homology and cellular approximation
                .modal-body
                    
                    p In this note we describe the role of the Schur multiplier in the structure of the $p$-torsion of discrete groups. More concretely, we show how the knowledge of $H_2G$ allows to approximate many groups by colimits of copies of finite $p$-groups. Our examples include interesting families of non-commutative infinite groups, including Burnside groups, certain solvable examples and the first Grigorchuk group. We also provide a counterexample for a conjecture of E. Farjoun.
                    
